<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mạc Kính Vũ</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Mac Kinh Vu</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Mạc Kính Vũ was the last ruler of the Mạc dynasty's enclave at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cao-bang">Cao Bằng</a> in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vietnam">Vietnam</a>. After the Mạc supported the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/revolt-of-the-three-feudatories">Revolt of the Three Feudatories</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>, the Qing withdrew their protection, and in 1677 Trịnh forces conquered Cao Bằng. Mạc Kính Vũ fled to China, ending more than 150 years of Mạc rule in Vietnam.</p></div>
